WEBVTT

00:00:00.321 --> 00:00:08.376
Healthcare Quality Lab V7.0: design, review, execute, investigate and measure. Synthetic insurance only. This recording makes no model request.

00:00:08.513 --> 00:00:16.534
AI can author expectations, or design a scenario whose values come from the independent calculator. Those are different capabilities. Historical raw failures remain visible.

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:24.826
This is an authored control, not a newly generated AI test. The independent gate checks money, ledger, history and accounts. Approval remains a separate action.

00:00:25.813 --> 00:00:33.831
After explicit scripted engineering review, the control passes actual isolated HTTP execution. No interactive claim ledger is changed.

00:00:34.127 --> 00:00:42.149
Versioned requirements link to scenarios, individual assertions and current execution evidence. A what-if change identifies maintenance candidates without editing policy.

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:52.587
A trusted one-cent pricing fault is caught: expected 71200, observed 71201. The original function is restored and passes. Requests, responses and evidence hashes are retained.

00:00:52.711 --> 00:01:00.750
The wrong raw AI baseline earns no mutation score. Authored controls and calculator-backed AI scenarios have different budgets; survivors and exact witnesses remain inspectable.

00:01:00.844 --> 00:01:10.928
Earlier actual model/prompt measurements: all four raw answers were ineligible on this selected input. Calculator controls compiled without model calls. This is not a general model ranking.

00:01:10.987 --> 00:01:21.026
Review the six reports, exact test receipts, public source and checksummed release. Independent checks and explicit review make AI failures visible; no claim of flawless or production healthcare behavior.
